From 30880c7160dfbff3c30a55f006bf9be9bd993fc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blazerpaul15 <blazerpaul15@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 15:48:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] [ax_vrr] Add configurable dynamic refresh rate ranges

Introduce overlay-configurable refresh rate ranges for Axion dynamic mode.
Dynamic mode now separates the lower-power app range from the full dynamic
range, allowing devices to keep normal/low-demand apps within 60-90Hz while
selected apps can use the full 60-120Hz range.

Add configurable defaults for the dynamic max rate, low dynamic max rate,
and interactive refresh rate. Keep sysprops available as runtime override
knobs for testing and device tuning.

Move full-range and low-range app handling into resource arrays so future
package adjustments can be done from device overlays without touching
framework code. Manual and per-app refresh rate selections remain able to
use higher panel modes such as 144Hz and 165Hz.

Change-Id: I1ac51ac064d79bbd4cb8c675b97b0b4afe448ada
